---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import SealStage from '../components/SealStage.astro';
import Row from '../components/Row.astro';
import Tray from '../components/mocks/Tray.astro';
import Shelf from '../components/mocks/Shelf.astro';
import Inspector from '../components/mocks/Inspector.astro';
import PantryResults from '../components/mocks/PantryResults.astro';
import Recipe from '../components/mocks/Recipe.astro';
import Intelligence from '../components/Intelligence.astro';
import Pickle from '../components/Pickle.astro';
import Pro from '../components/Pro.astro';
import Questions from '../components/Questions.astro';
---
<Base title="NetRelish — Keep the pages that matter" description="NetRelish is a Mac browser with a pantry. Save any page with one key, keep each project in its own jar, and seal the ones you’ll need again — searchable and offline, on your Mac.">
  <main>
    <Hero><SealStage /></Hero>

    <Row id="how" eyebrow="Capture" h2="One key to save anything.">
      <p>Press <kbd>⌘</kbd><kbd>D</kbd> on any page, or share it from Safari or any app with a share sheet. It lands in Brine, right where you can see it. Nothing gets lost in a bookmarks folder again.</p>
      <Tray slot="mock" />
    </Row>
    <Row eyebrow="Sort" h2="Jars, not folders." flip>
      <p>Pick a jar on the Shelf and browse in it. Everything you seal there stays in that jar. Jars are where your projects live — clients, research, reading, whatever you’re working on this month. Every jar is its own profile: its own cookies, its own logins.</p>
      <p>Switch with <kbd>⌘</kbd><kbd>1</kbd> through <kbd>⌘</kbd><kbd>9</kbd>.</p>
      <Shelf slot="mock" />
    </Row>
    <Row eyebrow="Seal" h2="Seal it, and it’s yours.">
      <p>Sealing saves a complete snapshot, closes the tab, and runs the jar’s Recipe. The page is preserved exactly as you saw it and never changes.</p>
      <p>The tab count goes down. That’s the point.</p>
      <Inspector slot="mock" />
    </Row>
    <Row eyebrow="Search" h2="Search what you kept, not the whole internet." flip>
      <p>Every sealed page is indexed in full, on your Mac. Press <kbd>⌘</kbd><kbd>K</kbd> to find it, or search from Shortcuts. A sealed result opens the saved copy, so it works offline.</p>
      <PantryResults slot="mock" />
    </Row>
    <Row eyebrow="Recipes" h2="Workflows that run when you seal.">
      <p>NetRelish comes with a few Recipes, like Seal &amp; Summarize, which summarizes the page on your Mac. Pick one for a jar and it runs every time you seal there.</p>
      <p>Every Recipe is a Shortcut, so Siri and the rest of your Mac can run it too.</p>
      <Recipe slot="mock" />
    </Row>

    <Intelligence />
    <Pickle />
    <Pro />
    <Questions />
  </main>
</Base>
